# AI artifacts — private, never committed. The cc-suite PRIVATE block below
# covers the bridge (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .claude/, .agents/, .codex/,
# .mcp.json); these are the rest: plugin configs, the design notes, and the spikes kept
# beside them in dev-docs/spikes — throwaway investigations, not code XiaolaiDict ships.
# No spike is tracked and none is in the history, so code that learned something from one
# says which spike and which finding, never a path into this repository. Kept outside the
# cc-suite sentinels so cc-suite's own rewrites cannot drop them.
# Slash-free on purpose: a trailing slash matches only a directory, so a
# symlink to one (a git worktree linking back here) would show as untracked.
/.cc-suite.md
/.cc-suite
/.claude-english-buddy.json
/dev-docs

# Swift build output. Slash-free for the same reason as above: a worktree's symlink must match too.
/.build
# `.swiftpm` is Xcode's per-user state, except for `xcshareddata` — which is the part Xcode
# separates out precisely so it can be committed. The shared XiaolaiDictUI scheme lives there, and
# previews do not work without it: ignoring the whole directory meant a fresh clone opened
# Package.swift and found nothing to preview.
/.swiftpm/*
!/.swiftpm/xcode
/.swiftpm/xcode/*
!/.swiftpm/xcode/xcshareddata
# Python's bytecode cache, written when the icon generator's tests import it.
__pycache__
# Ruff's cache, written wherever it is run. Unanchored and slash-free like `__pycache__`.
.ruff_cache

# Secrets. Unanchored on purpose, unlike the build directories above: a `.env` is dangerous
# wherever it lands — inside a spike or a tool's folder as much as at the root — and a rule
# that matched only at the root would miss exactly the one that leaks. `.env.*` also covers
# `.env.example`; if a checked-in template is ever wanted, add `!.env.example` after these.
.env
.env.*

# >>> cc-suite >>>
# cc-suite-schema: 8
# AI assistant local state
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/*.local.*
CLAUDE.local.md

# Codex CLI — local files, keep checked-in subdirs
.codex/*
!.codex/skills/
!.codex/prompts/
!.codex/hooks.json
!.codex/hooks.cc-suite.json
!.codex/config.toml

# cc-suite-managed symlinks (created by bridge_skills.sh) — derived, not authored
.claude/skills/cc-suite
.agents/skills

# Antigravity workspace MCP config is generated from .mcp.json and may contain
# credentials or machine-specific paths.
.agents/mcp_config.json
.agents/.cc-suite-mcp.provenance.json

# cc-suite tool-profile bridge (grok/opencode/qwen) — derived provenance
# sidecars tracking which MCP servers cc-suite owns. Not authored.
.cc-suite-*.provenance.json

# cc-suite local state — what init created, and the pre-bridge CLAUDE.md backup.
# Machine-local bookkeeping, not shared. Listed file-by-file on purpose:
# .cc-suite/agents/ holds declared advisors and IS meant to be committed.
.cc-suite/provenance
.cc-suite/original-claude.md
# Audit findings files written by /cc-suite:audit and the audit-fix loop —
# per-run working state (findings + fix statuses), not authored content.
.cc-suite/audits/

# cc-suite: PRIVATE mode — bridge artifacts not shared
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.mcp.json
# <<< cc-suite <<<

# Corpus extraction — the whole directory, scripts and output alike, stays local. The corpus is
# copyrighted dictionary text and is never committed. Slash-free for the same reason as the rules
# above: a trailing slash matches only a directory, so a symlink to one would show as untracked.
/Tools/corpus
